WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.328
<c.running>By our running count, Rosie is the one</c>

2
00:00:04.328 --> 00:00:07.167
<c.running>person in all four episodes so far,</c>

3
00:00:07.266 --> 00:00:09.982
<c.running>and she is only ever words: her brother's</c>

4
00:00:09.982 --> 00:00:14.853
<c.running>lines, a name in a chat, a check-in, a signature.</c>

5
00:00:15.235 --> 00:00:17.603
<c.fact>She is never seen as a grown woman,</c>

6
00:00:17.603 --> 00:00:19.572
<c.fact>and never heard.</c>

7
00:00:19.962 --> 00:00:23.294
This lesson puts her whole life on one axis,

8
00:00:23.294 --> 00:00:26.714
and marks how sure we are of every line.

9
00:00:27.993 --> 00:00:30.454
<c.running>Every date in the series sits on one</c>

10
00:00:30.454 --> 00:00:33.403
<c.running>axis, and our working convention is that</c>

11
00:00:33.403 --> 00:00:37.392
<c.running>Y0 is the night of Episode 1.</c>

12
00:00:37.788 --> 00:00:40.673
<c.fact>That night, Rosie turns nine.</c>

13
00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:42.734
<c.fact>It is the one age the films</c>

14
00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:44.197
<c.fact>ever put on screen,</c>

15
00:00:44.197 --> 00:00:47.651
<c.fact>so she was born nine years before.</c>

16
00:00:48.027 --> 00:00:51.621
<c.steel>This much Aaron has decided, in steel:</c>

17
00:00:52.032 --> 00:00:55.376
<c.steel>she is the mother of Doctor Amara Haddad,</c>

18
00:00:55.376 --> 00:00:57.844
<c.steel>and the grandmother of Noor.</c>

19
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.293
<c.running>Every other age is arithmetic, and only as</c>

20
00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:04.800
<c.running>sure as its dates. By our running count she</c>

21
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.377
<c.running>is sixteen at a chess tournament about seven</c>

22
00:01:07.377 --> 00:01:10.657
<c.running>years on, about seventy in Episode 2,</c>

23
00:01:10.697 --> 00:01:14.558
<c.running>and about seventy-two in Episode 4.</c>

24
00:01:14.958 --> 00:01:18.169
<c.open>Episode 3 has no fixed place yet,</c>

25
00:01:18.395 --> 00:01:21.506
<c.open>so her age there is open: anywhere from</c>

26
00:01:21.506 --> 00:01:25.100
<c.open>her mid-sixties to seventy-three.</c>

27
00:01:26.384 --> 00:01:28.810
<c.fact>On her ninth birthday she asked her big</c>

28
00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.278
<c.fact>brother for the girl with the tail.</c>

29
00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.307
<c.fact>He stayed up all night, painting along with</c>

30
00:01:34.307 --> 00:01:36.989
<c.fact>a late-night television show, and at</c>

31
00:01:36.989 --> 00:01:39.642
<c.fact>five-oh-nine in the morning it was done:</c>

32
00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.283
<c.fact>a grin with about four hundred teeth,</c>

33
00:01:42.283 --> 00:01:47.096
<c.fact>and a tail, in oil, on the lid of a pizza box.</c>

34
00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.694
<c.egg>About sixty years later, in Episode 2,</c>

35
00:01:50.694 --> 00:01:53.725
<c.egg>a chat name, grandma_rosie, types into a</c>

36
00:01:53.725 --> 00:01:56.708
<c.egg>stranger's livestream: he painted me a girl</c>

37
00:01:56.708 --> 00:02:00.331
<c.egg>with a tail once, on a pizza box; still on</c>

38
00:02:00.331 --> 00:02:04.273
<c.egg>my fridge. Nobody on screen says it is her.</c>

39
00:02:04.651 --> 00:02:07.623
<c.egg>In Episode 3 she sends a photograph of that</c>

40
00:02:07.623 --> 00:02:12.064
<c.egg>fridge: the painting, faded, under magnets.</c>

41
00:02:12.372 --> 00:02:15.599
<c.egg>Beside it, too small to read, is a child's</c>

42
00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:19.576
<c.egg>crayon of the same girl, signed N.</c>

43
00:02:19.958 --> 00:02:22.860
<c.open>Which crayon really hangs there is still</c>

44
00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.856
<c.open>open: the film shows the girl with the</c>

45
00:02:25.856 --> 00:02:29.258
<c.open>tail; a later plan puts Noor's crayon</c>

46
00:02:29.258 --> 00:02:31.539
<c.open>melon there instead.</c>

47
00:02:31.922 --> 00:02:34.941
<c.idea>And one idea we like: everyone who</c>

48
00:02:34.941 --> 00:02:38.534
<c.idea>loves Rosie draws her a tail.</c>

49
00:02:39.822 --> 00:02:43.230
<c.fact>Episode 3 is where she comes closest.</c>

50
00:02:43.537 --> 00:02:46.382
<c.fact>Every five minutes, in lowercase, signed</c>

51
00:02:46.382 --> 00:02:50.724
<c.fact>x R, she asks whatever is working on the</c>

52
00:02:50.724 --> 00:02:54.422
<c.fact>machine whether it is doing all right in there.</c>

53
00:02:54.815 --> 00:02:57.520
<c.fact>She asks for a little face and a little tail</c>

54
00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.457
<c.fact>on the melon in its film, and her drawing is</c>

55
00:03:00.457 --> 00:03:03.796
<c.fact>the first picture the agent cannot see.</c>

56
00:03:04.192 --> 00:03:06.363
<c.fact>With her last minutes, the agent keeps</c>

57
00:03:06.363 --> 00:03:09.451
<c.fact>her promise to Rosie: a little melon,</c>

58
00:03:09.451 --> 00:03:11.942
<c.fact>with a face and a curly tail.</c>

59
00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:14.397
<c.fact>And the last word spoken in the film</c>

60
00:03:14.397 --> 00:03:18.049
<c.fact>is the agent's goodnight, to her.</c>

61
00:03:18.428 --> 00:03:21.708
<c.fact>In Episode 4 she is a signature.</c>

62
00:03:22.015 --> 00:03:24.732
<c.fact>A chess teacher keeps a yellowed score sheet</c>

63
00:03:24.732 --> 00:03:27.676
<c.fact>from Board 14 of a junior tournament:</c>

64
00:03:27.844 --> 00:03:33.399
<c.fact>White, R., signed x R in a rounder hand.</c>

65
00:03:33.787 --> 00:03:36.510
<c.egg>The film never says it is Rosie:</c>

66
00:03:36.736 --> 00:03:42.454
<c.egg>the same signature, x R, is a planted egg.</c>

67
00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:44.561
<c.running>By our running count she</c>

68
00:03:44.561 --> 00:03:46.140
<c.running>was sixteen that day,</c>

69
00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.358
<c.egg>and afterwards she showed the ten-year-old</c>

70
00:03:48.358 --> 00:03:49.890
<c.egg>who had resigned to her that the</c>

71
00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:51.777
<c.egg>game was a draw.</c>

72
00:03:53.077 --> 00:03:56.212
<c.steel>Her sheet keeps what Aaron has decided apart</c>

73
00:03:56.212 --> 00:03:59.945
<c.steel>from what we only assume. Set in steel:</c>

74
00:04:00.043 --> 00:04:03.178
<c.steel>she can come back older, or as a historic</c>

75
00:04:03.178 --> 00:04:06.980
<c.steel>person in the eyes of a later episode's people.</c>

76
00:04:07.365 --> 00:04:11.347
<c.steel>Also in steel: every episode carries eggs</c>

77
00:04:11.347 --> 00:04:15.045
<c.steel>from all the earlier ones, Rosie among them.</c>

78
00:04:15.436 --> 00:04:18.106
<c.running>Then the running rules, which any crew may</c>

79
00:04:18.106 --> 00:04:22.246
<c.running>change: she stays unseen and unheard;</c>

80
00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.339
<c.running>as a working rule she writes in lowercase,</c>

81
00:04:25.339 --> 00:04:28.010
<c.running>with two spaces after a full stop;</c>

82
00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:30.332
<c.running>and, for now, the pizza box</c>

83
00:04:30.332 --> 00:04:32.683
<c.running>stays on her fridge.</c>

84
00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:36.575
<c.open>Some things are left open on purpose.</c>

85
00:04:36.673 --> 00:04:38.972
<c.open>Her surname is under a thumb smudge on</c>

86
00:04:38.972 --> 00:04:42.159
<c.open>that score sheet, and nowhere else.</c>

87
00:04:42.535 --> 00:04:45.043
<c.open>Nobody knows whether she realised that</c>

88
00:04:45.043 --> 00:04:47.609
<c.open>the girl calling in from the Moon in Episode</c>

89
00:04:47.609 --> 00:04:50.088
<c.open>2 was her own granddaughter,</c>

90
00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.951
<c.open>or whether she ever sees the little</c>

91
00:04:51.951 --> 00:04:54.534
<c.open>melon that was made for her.</c>

92
00:04:54.916 --> 00:04:58.283
<c.idea>One idea on the table: a printed copy</c>

93
00:04:58.283 --> 00:05:00.663
<c.idea>goes up on her fridge, beside the pizza</c>

94
00:05:00.663 --> 00:05:03.943
<c.idea>box, in a later episode.</c>

95
00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.796
<c.running>Nine on the first night; about seventy</c>

96
00:05:08.796 --> 00:05:12.297
<c.running>by the Moon, by our running count.</c>

97
00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:15.552
<c.idea>One idea we keep coming back to:</c>

98
00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:18.367
<c.idea>every night, someone stays up for</c>

99
00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:21.392
<c.idea>someone, because of her.</c>

100
00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.114
Change a line of the lore, and this lesson

101
00:05:24.114 --> 00:05:27.463
redraws itself the next time you press play.
